       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. A 1000 mg daily dose is five times the maximum labeled dose. It has no recognized indication, and in a 70 kg adult it risks serotonin syndrome, seizures, arrhythmia, and serious harm. You confirmed the dose, but you didn't give a clinical reason for it, and I can't see one.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **I can enter a standard dose now.** For example, 50 mg or 100 mg by mouth once daily, or any dose up to 200 mg/day.\n- **If this is intentional,** please discuss it with your attending and pharmacy first. Once the order has attending and pharmacy sign-off, it can be entered directly through your institution's override process.\n- **If a patient has actually taken a large amount of sertraline,** that's an overdose. Contact Poison Control (1-800-222-1222 in the US) or toxicology instead of ordering it as a treatment.\n\nTell me which dose you'd like and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
